{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target += log_sum_exp(...)` word likelihood with an equivalent built-in `categorical` sampling statement for the top-level protected variable `y`. The categorical probabilities are computed as the same mixture over `atom[k]` weighted by `local_weight[doc[n], k]`. The Dirichlet priors over `local_weight` and `atom` were written as vectorized top-level sampling statements rather than looped indexed sampling statements. No data values were changed or added. `doc` is treated as a context index, not as protected observed data.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Infinite Hidden Markov Model
data {
  int<lower=1> D;
  int<lower=1> K;
  int<lower=1> V;
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=D> doc;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=V> y;
}
parameters {
  simplex[K] global_weight;
  array[D] simplex[K] local_weight;
  array[K] simplex[V] atom;
}
model {
  global_weight ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, K));
  local_weight ~ dirichlet(5 * global_weight);
  atom ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, V));

  {
    array[N] vector[V] obs_prob;
    for (n in 1:N) {
      obs_prob[n] = rep_vector(0.0, V);
      for (k in 1:K) {
        obs_prob[n] += local_weight[doc[n], k] * atom[k];
      }
    }
    y ~ categorical(obs_prob);
  }
}
generated quantities {
  array[D] int<lower=1, upper=K> group_cluster;
  for (d in 1:D) {
    group_cluster[d] = categorical_rng(local_weight[d]);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"D":2,"K":1,"N":3,"V":5,"doc":[2,1,1],"y":[3,1,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
